  "description": "Amendments to planning permission dated 17 May 2024 (RN 23/08027/FULL) for SITE COMPRISING 53-63 NEW BOND STREET/5-17/17A BROOK STREET: Alteration and extension of the existing buildings, including partial demolition and retention and retrofit to provide a building with basement, ground and ten upper floors, setback at fifth to eighth floors with terraces, setback at ninth floor with terrace and plant, and a roof terrace with lift over run and pavilion at the tenth floor, with satellite dish, green roof and solar photo voltaic panels on its roof, and associated works, to provide for retail (Class E (a)) and office (Class E(g)(i)) uses together with associated ancillary spaces to those uses. NAMELY, amendments to planning permission dated 17th May 2024 (RN 23/08027/FULL) comprising minor refinements to terrace balustrades and planters; window and grille adjustments to the south and east elevations; removal of the chimney at 55, 53 New Bond Street; installation of an emergency generator flue; revisions to the glazing and signage band to Retail Unit 3; window adjustments to Levels 4 and 5 on the Brook Street elevation; and the addition of a lightweight canopy, roof hatch and safety barrier at Level 10.",
